description:
Port upstream's safety-net wrap from Markdown.render (pi-mono markdown.ts:152-158).

After all tokens are rendered into lines, wrap every line through WrapAnsi.wrap(line, content_width) before adding margins. This catches list items, headings, code blocks, and any other node that doesn't respect width.

Current state: render_node for ol/ul ignores _width entirely (markdown.ex:124-131). render_list_items doesn't receive width at all. Headings (h1-h6) don't wrap. Code block lines aren't truncated.

Upstream pattern (markdown.ts:152-158):
```typescript
const wrappedLines: string[] = [];
for (const line of renderedLines) {
    wrappedLines.push(...wrapTextWithAnsi(line, contentWidth));
}
```

Apply between the token rendering loop and the margin/padding step in our do_render/1.
